        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: let plugins control inbound debounce policy",
        "body": "Related: #54565\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nPlugins cannot currently decide whether rich inbound WhatsApp messages should bypass debounce or choose a debounce window for a specific account, DM, group, conversation, or sender. Doing either requires changing product defaults or adding more core configuration.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds a typed `inbound_debounce` plugin hook. The hook receives the channel's default action, duration, a read-only debounce key, conversation context, and media/location/quote facts. It may explicitly debounce, bypass, or select a duration.\n\nWhatsApp now consults this hook while preserving its current defaults. Control commands still dispatch immediately. Rich batches preserve all media and structured context, and split safely when multiple quotes or locations cannot be represented without data loss.\n\nThis is an API-based alternative to the product-level approaches in #103049 and #100970. It lets plugins provide those policies without adding native product settings.\n\nAI-assisted with Codex.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThere is no behavior change when no plugin implements the hook. Plugins can opt media, locations, or quoted replies into batching and can choose different windows for DMs, groups, accounts, conversations, senders, or their own policy scopes.\n\nThe hook is bounded by a two-second timeout, preserves per-conversation arrival order, keeps control commands immediate, and cannot replace the debounce key to merge unrelated conversations.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent head: `5efc62e9898`\nCurrent base merged: `44f20956e33`\n\n- `node scripts/plugin-sdk-surface-report.mjs --check`: passed with 8,152 public exports and no forbidden subpaths.\n- `node --import tsx scripts/generate-bundled-channel-config-metadata.ts --check`: passed.\n- Focused Vitest proof: 4 shards, 185 tests passed across inbound debounce, WhatsApp dispatch, WhatsApp connection/logging E2E, and config schema coverage.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Fresh full-branch autoreview against `origin/main`: no accepted or actionable findings.\n\nReal installed-plugin WhatsApp proof is still needed, and maintainers still need to choose this plugin-hook contract or the competing conversation-config approach in #100970.\n",
